working_notes/failed_attempts.md:51:Lesson: \(\Psi\) is useful lower-bound/Bayes-value language, but exact characterization must first be proved on finite \(\Theta\) and finite \(G\) with grid-restricted comparator \(V_\theta^G\). The continuum passage is approximate and must carry \(O(T/K)\)-type errors.
